  "question": {
    "text": "Five charges $+q,+5 q,-2 q,+3 q$ and $-4 q$ are situated as shown in the figure, The electric flux due to this configuration through the surface S is :\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0006_6310416784cf.png\"/><br/>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{5 q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{4 q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3 q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Using Gauss's law, $\\phi=\\frac{q}{\\epsilon_0}$\nHere, $\\mathrm{q}=$ charge inside the closed surface\n$\\therefore \\phi=\\frac{q+(-2 q)+5 q}{\\epsilon_0}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\phi=\\frac{4 q}{\\epsilon_0}$"
  }
}